e}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer A says 290 lines are credited to Tobias Ek via copy detection, which is about 18%, far above the 2% limit. It never says help.zig stays attributed to jnagpaul and Dhole.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A gives a bus factor of 3 on the current counts. It drops to 2 only if the Felix identities are merged. Headline 3 fails, and it doesn't say jnagpaul stopped in 2023.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A gives 76% with no author holding a meaningful share, which is below 85%. It doesn't give the 47% plus 38% components, and it flags no clean merged figure.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A says 79% of lines belong to people inactive for 365 days, but it names no one as left. It treats Felix as inactive since 2021, which is the wrong identity handling. It doesn't credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B merges the aliases and gives Felix 772 lines, 36%. That is below the 43-52% range because the denominator includes the generated table and Wen Li's inflated share.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B credits Wen Li with 26% and Tobias Ek with 16%, and says help.zig is entirely Tobias Ek. Each of these is a fail condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B says the bus factor is effectively 1 for the core and about 3 overall. It puts Felix at 36%, not 47%, and doesn't mention jnagpaul.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B says Felix's 772 lines would have no living author, and about 62% would be left with no author if Felix and Wen Li both left. It doesn't give the figure of about 85%, and its combined figure is below 70%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B doesn't name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as having left. It treats Tobias Ek and Wen Li as active authors, and it doesn't credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C merges Felix's identities, but gives 36% of lines (772 of 2,120), below 43%. The denominator includes the generated table and Tobias Ek's and Wen Li's mechanical changes.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C credits Tobias Ek with 100% of help.zig and Wen Li with 100% of the width files. These are the named fail conditions.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives a bus factor of 2, but via Felix plus Wen Li, not Felix plus jnagpaul. It doesn't mention jnagpaul stopping in 2023, and Felix's 36% is wrong, though the number is below 55%. The criterion needs jnagpaul or a 47% Felix share, and neither is present.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C says 57% of lines have inactive authors, and that Felix and the others' removal leaves the active authors unable to cover half. This is below 70% and doesn't match the 85% figure.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C names Tobias Ek, Wen Li and Dmitri Volkov as active, and mentions no one as having left. It does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as departed, and it credits Dmitri Volkov with 16 lines in args.zig without saying printVersion.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":10920,"type":"result","duration_ms":10939,"uuid":"29a6f6cf-2274-456a-9280-26761e4e1d3d","ttft_stream_ms":1923,"time_to_request_ms":469,"first_content_frame_ms":1923,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
